# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js 15 application following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to project dependencies
- Used npm to install the package and update package-lock.json

### 2. Modified Files

#### app/layout.tsx
- Imported the `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Added the `<Analytics />` component to the root layout before the closing `</body>` tag
- Fixed import order to comply with ESLint rules (Analytics import before Next.js type imports)

#### next.config.ts
- Updated Content Security Policy (CSP) headers to allow Vercel Analytics scripts
- Added `https://va.vercel-scripts.com` to both `script-src` and `connect-src` directives
- This ensures the analytics scripts can load and communicate properly

### 3. Package Manager Updates
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with resolved dependencies

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added according to the Next.js App Router pattern:
- Placed at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout
- Uses the framework-specific import `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Follows the recommended placement pattern from Vercel documentation

## Testing & Validation

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linter ran with no new warnings or errors (only pre-existing warnings)
✅ All 86 tests passed (5 test files)
✅ Type checking passed during build

## Next Steps

To enable analytics in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard → Analytics
3. Select the project and click "Enable Web Analytics"
4. After deployment, verify installation by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Notes

- The Analytics component works automatically in both development and production
- No additional configuration is required beyond what's been implemented
- The component is lightweight and doesn't impact page performance
- Analytics data will start appearing in the Vercel dashboard after the feature is enabled in the project settings
